00:00:02.720 --> 00:00:03.350 align:start position:0%
 
hi  my name is eric sachman and i'm the  associate director of applications  engineering here at broken lights  i'm going to talk to you today about how  our new optoplasma b  discovery workflow will accelerate lead  molecule discovery  against difficult targets  and i'll be making some forward-looking  statements in this presentation  even the best athletes in the world know  that they have to take multiple shots on  target  in order to hit the mark in hockey top  scorers may need to take over 100 shots  on goal  as a result these athletes aim to  generate high volumes  of high quality shots in an effort to  win every game  drug discovery also requires a large  number of shots on target  in order to yield an effect an effective  therapeutic molecule  by some estimates less than five percent  of drug discovery campaigns  successfully successfully yield a new  therapeutic  and unlike professional sports this  inefficiency is extremely problematic  because each campaign can take over a  decade and cost over a billion dollars  success rates for therapeutic antibody  discovery against difficult targets  has been especially poor since these  antibodies often  need to bind cryptic epitopes or trigger  complex molecular functions  to date only one out of an estimated 800  human gpcrs  has an approved antibody uh  antibody therapeutic  to close the gap drug discover drug  discovery developers  need to find ways to increase the  quantity quality and speed  of lead generation  berkelights's optoplasmb discovery  workflows can yield hits against  difficult membrane targets like  gpcrs genovec has successfully  discovered antibodies against  three transmembrane proteins that  exemplify the common problems with  difficult targets  small extracellular regions reducing the  number of possible sites to target  high sequence homology reducing the  chances of eliciting an immune response  and  by extension likely lower frequency of  antigen-specific b  cells and poor surface cell surface  expression  making a cell-based screening difficult  across all three targets they've found  approximately 10 times  more hits than the traditional  traditional hybridoma campaign  i'm going to describe to you how our  newest  optoplasma b discovery workflow expands  on these capabilities to accelerate  lead selection molecules excuse me  selection of lead molecules against  difficult targets  antibody discovery using the traditional  hybridoma approach requires  immortalization of b  cells by cell fusion followed by a  lengthy process of expansion  sub cloning and screening the  immortalization step  often results in the death of greater  than 90 of b-cells and therefore results  in a significant loss  of b-cell diversity  new single b-cell technologies seek to  access greater cell diversity by  bypassing the cell fusion  however many of these approaches provide  little or no functional information  this results in significant time labor  and expense for  sequencing cloning re-expression and  characterizing irrelevant antibodies  that do not bind the correct epitope or  fail to demonstrate the desired function  optoplasma b discovery 4.0 maximizes  diversity of antibodies through direct  functional profiling  of plasma b cells from immunized mice  the workflow enables users to recover  thousands of hits by screening broad b  cell diversity  down select lead candidates by  functional profiling  sequence and re-express over 1000  antibodies for  less than 100 per molecule all in a week  the workflow begins with the loading of  a plasma b cell sample  onto berkeley lights's beacon  optoflytics system  the beacon system fully automates cell  sample handling  screening cdna synthesis and sequence  recovery  a 96 well play containing a purified  plasma b cell sample  is inserted onto the beacon  the beacon system then automatically  loads the cell sample  onto optoselect chips  each optical select chip contains over  20 000 nanopens  each less than a nanoliter in volume  that's greater than 10 000 times  smaller than a well in an isix well  plate  plasma b cells are cloned into nanopens  using berkely's optoselect technology  in which cells are manipulated by light  as shown here the light based  manipulation can be selectively  performed on cells with markers for  viability or  other phenotypic information  tens of thousands of plasma b cells from  the target population can be cloned  across multiple chips in under four  hours  nanopins enable rapid precise and highly  sensitive assays  the small volumes enable secreted  antibody concentrations  to reach detectable levels in a matter  of minutes  in the assay depicted on this slide  secreted antibodies from the plasma b  cells  bind antigen-coated beads and are  detected by  binding of secondary antibody this  results  in a fluorescent halo above the pens  containing antigen-specific  plasma b cells this assay is performed  on tens of thousands of cells  simultaneously  the video on the slide depicts a single  field of view in which hundreds of cells  are  are screened to identify dozens of  targets  or excuse me dozens of hits  antibody specificity and cross  reactivity can be assessed by performing  multiple  assays either sequentially or in  parallel  in this figure we depict three assays  running in parallel  and simultaneously identifying that  there  are antibodies that are specific to  androgen y  antibodies that are cross reactive to  both androgen x and  antigen y as well as antibodies that are  specific to  uh not that are not specific to either  antigen  cell binding assays can be used to  enable down selection of leaked  candidates  against difficult membrane targets  in these assays beads are replaced with  cells that are over expressing the  target antigen on the cell surface  antibodies specific to the cell surface  target are  again selected based on the fluorescent  halos at the top of the pens  containing antigen specific plasma b  cells  following the single plasma b cell  cloning and assays to identify  the antigen specific antibodies optoseq  barcoded bcr is used to automate the  sequence recovery  mrna capture beads with dual genetic and  optical barcodes  are loaded into specific pens and plasma  b cells are lysed to capture the mrna  reverse transcription is then performed  on chip to generate the stable cdna  following the cdna synthesis the optical  barcodes for each bead  are read out by fluorescence imaging  the optical barcodes are stored in  software to subsequently link  each antibody sequence to its function  the barcode beads are then automatically  recovered in bulk  over a thousand hits can be recovered in  a single 96 well plate  and additional hits can be recovered in  multiple well plates if the user desires  using this technology we demonstrated  the recovery of nearly 12 000 hits  from two optoplasma b discovery  workflows performed in a week  from a single plasma b cell sample  using a combination of fragmentation  next gen sequencing  and bioinformatics analysis optoc  barcoded bcr enables rapid and accurate  sequencing  of the full length variable regions of  antibody genes  the ability to reconstruct full-length  antibody genes from short reads  enables high throughput sequencing of  over a thousand antibodies from a single  run  on a standard alumina sequencing  platform  as the graph on this slide shows over  500 paired  heavy and light chain antibody sequences  were recovered from a single 9612 plate  and performing a single mysq run  production of lead molecules for  downstream characterization  typically includes costly gene synthesis  and laborious bacterial cloning  opto bcr rapid re-expression  enables production of antibodies in just  one week  to confirm function in a play-based  assay  amplified cdna is cloned directly into  re-expression constructs  enabling expression of over 1000  antibodies  for rapid functional confirmation  in this graph greater than 80 percent of  the over 250 re-expressed antibodies  exhibited antigen specificity  in plate-based elisa assays  the new optoplasma b discovery workflow  advances from b  cells to lead molecules in just a week  the workflow enables recovery of  thousands of hits by screening broad  b-cell diversity  down selection of lead candidates by  functional profiling  sequencing and re-expression of over  1000 functionally characterized  antibodies  by increasing the quantity quality and  speed of generating shots on goal  berkelight's optoplasma b discovery  workflow  will enable drug developers to discover  lead candidates  against difficult targets  thank you and please reach out if you're  interested in learning more

